{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And I, here, I have given you.</b> In joy — this is an expression of joy, as in ״הִנֵּה הוּא יֹצֵא לִקְרָאתֶךָ וְרָאֲךָ וְשָׂמַח בְּלִבּוֹ״ (Exodus 4). A parable: a king who gave a field to his friend, and did not write or seal or register it in the records. Someone came and contested the field. The king said to him: whoever wishes may come and contest against you — here I am writing and sealing for you and registering in the records. So too here: because Korah came and contested against Aaron regarding the priesthood, Scripture came and gave him 24 priestly gifts in a covenant of salt forever. And therefore this section is joined here (Sifrei)." "<b>The charge of My terumah.</b> That you must guard them in purity." "<b>For anointing.</b> For greatness (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:32.331819962Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}